# A shift by a runtime count emits a counted loop; the historical bug
# dropped it (`1 << idx` became `lda.w #1`). Offsets follow the
# left-to-right ABI: the count is the last-pushed argument, and `pha` of
# the value moves it 2 bytes further (ported from opensnes-emu
# test_variable_shift, strengthened with the loop shape).
in shift_left_var: present lda 6,s\n\tpha\n\tlda 6,s\n\ttax\n\tpla\n\tcpx #0\n\tbeq \+\n-\tasl a\n\tdex\n\tbne -
in shift_right_var: present lda 6,s\n\tpha\n\tlda 6,s\n\ttax\n\tpla\n\tcpx #0\n\tbeq \+\n-\tlsr a\n\tdex\n\tbne -
# 1 << idx: the constant 1 is shifted, the count is the only argument.
in compute_bitmask: present lda\.w #1\n\tpha\n\tlda 6,s\n\ttax\n\tpla\n\tcpx #0\n\tbeq \+\n-\tasl a
# (reg >> shift) & mask: reg at 8,s, shift at 6,s (+2 after pha), mask at 4,s.
in extract_field: present lda 8,s\n\tpha\n\tlda 8,s\n\ttax\n\tpla
in extract_field: present -\tlsr a\n\tdex\n\tbne -\n\+\n\tand 4,s
